.TH "REPROCTL\-AUTONOMY" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-autonomy \- durable local claim, monitor, and sequencing state
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl autonomy\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage durable local state for autonomous orchestration.
.PP
The \f[B]sequence\f[R] subcommand asks OpenCode to rank candidate issues
before planning and execution.
It uses monitor eligibility as the baseline, then writes a durable
prompt, raw response, and canonical JSON artifact set under
\f[B]tmp/autonomy/sequences/\f[R].
.PP
The sequencing stage is intentionally narrower than the autonomous
runner.
It does not launch agents, mutate Linear, or create worktrees.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]sequence\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-limit\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-profile\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-prompt\-file\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-output\-dir\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-claimed\-by\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Build a candidate evaluation from the current backlog/todo issues,
render a prompt, run OpenCode, and write durable sequencing artifacts.
The default prompt lives at
\f[B]scripts/lib/prompts/autonomy\-sequence.md\f[R].
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-limit\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]
Limit the candidate evaluation passed into sequencing.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-profile\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Pass a specific OpenCode profile to the launcher.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-prompt\-file\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Use an alternate sequencing prompt template.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-output\-dir\f[R] \f[I]path\f[R]
Override the sequencing artifact directory.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-claimed\-by\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]
Tag the candidate evaluation with the active operator name.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Emit the canonical sequencing JSON instead of a short text summary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl autonomy sequence \-\-limit 2 \-\-profile github\-copilot\-sonnet \-\-output\-dir tmp/autonomy/sequences \-\-json
Generate a durable sequencing artifact set for the next planning wave.
